# Commands run by the launchd job com.hakios.demo for the shutter check.
# The scene opens Camera.app as rc.jobs.camera does -- SpringBoard's first frame
# takes minutes, so the tap waits 300 s, then the Camera icon at 0.845 0.36 --
# and waits 165 s for the app (its preview comes about 130 s after the tap;
# logs/120653-run.log armed the session at kernel t 435 with the location
# consent alert up at 440, camera108-440.png).  Camera.app now asks for the
# location when it starts, because location services answer: the alert's
# "Allow While Using App" is at 0.500 0.699, the same place Weather's had.  It
# is tapped twice -- the first may come before the alert has animated in, and a
# tap with no alert on screen only sets the preview's focus.  Then the shutter
# is tapped three times: it is the white circle at the screen's centre-bottom,
# 0.500 0.866 (camui2-600.png), and a photograph is the capture stack's
# StillImageCaptureNow, which the media layer answers with eight whole-sensor
# frames summed (camera_device.c, still_accumulate()).  Three, because the
# capture graph restarts the stream for the first photograph and a request that
# arrives with that restart is dropped: logs/121949-run.log's first request
# came with "the frames for iOS stopped (closed)" and only the second was
# given; the taps 50 s apart leave room for the eight frames and the encode.
# No flip tap: every photograph is the wide S5KHMX's.
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 300 swipe 0.5 0.99 0.5 0.4 250 wait 3 tap 0.845 0.36 wait 165 tap 0.5 0.699 wait 10 tap 0.5 0.699 wait 10 tap 0.5 0.866 wait 50 tap 0.5 0.866 wait 50 tap 0.5 0.866 wait 30
